From d698194841950ec7d2edc12877e9564dee3dcd26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:18:54 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 64/78] PlaitOS: adapt Smart Pixels to GrapheneOS

- Keys are Settings.Secure plait_smart_pixel_filter_enabled (default off)
  and plait_smart_pixel_filter_percent instead of new Settings API constants
- The tile is registered by a new SmartPixelModule (crDroid uses LineageOS's
  LineageModule) and listed in quick_settings_tiles_stock, so it can be added
  in the tile editor; strings go to plait_strings.xml
- The pattern shifts by one pixel each minute through all 64 positions of
  its 8x8 tile, as the original OmniROM/DU Smart Pixels did: with a fixed
  pattern the always-lit pixels age faster and can leave a faint grid on the
  OLED, which defeats the burn-in purpose
- No recycle() of the replaced pattern bitmap: the render thread may still be
  drawing with it (recycled-bitmap crash); it is 8x8 pixels, GC is enough

crDroid's follow-up that turns Smart Pixels off during UDFPS scans (64f88200b,
config default off there too) is not ported: it rewrites the saved setting
around each scan. Revisit if fingerprint unlock suffers with it on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
